# FlyEnv Solution pages

When creating, rewriting, reviewing, or materially expanding any FlyEnv `/solutions/` page, **MUST use the `flyenv-designing-solution-pages` skill before changing the page structure or content.**

Rules that remain mandatory even under batch/fast-edit requests:

- Keep the FlyEnv design system consistent; do not standardize Solution-page information architecture.
- Treat the Laravel Solution page as a quality reference, never as a universal template.
- Produce a compact Page Strategy before implementation.
- Require at least 2–3 technology-specific primary sections.
- Run the Name Replacement Test before completion.
- Keep Solution search intent distinct from existing Guide pages.
- Prefer real FlyEnv workflows, UI, architecture and project-specific proof over generic framework introductions or SEO filler.
- Do not force Comparison or FAQ sections onto every page.
